WEBVTT

00:03.920 --> 00:04.280
Okay.

00:04.280 --> 00:04.800
Moving on.

00:04.800 --> 00:06.520
We have a lot of use cases for the views.

00:06.520 --> 00:07.680
They are just amazing.

00:07.680 --> 00:14.400
So the next one is we can use views in order to introduce a second version of my data model in another

00:14.400 --> 00:17.800
language, so we could offer multiple languages to the users.

00:17.840 --> 00:19.240
Let's understand what this means.

00:19.240 --> 00:20.560
So now we have the following scenario.

00:20.600 --> 00:25.840
We have again our table orders where the data is persisted and everything in English.

00:25.840 --> 00:31.440
And of course what happens sometimes you have like international team that are accessing your data.

00:31.440 --> 00:35.000
So you have team in USA and maybe you have team from Germany.

00:35.000 --> 00:38.280
That as well are end users that want to access the data.

00:38.320 --> 00:42.160
Of course, it depends on the number of users that are using your database.

00:42.160 --> 00:47.960
But if you have a lot of users that come from Germany and as well from India, it might make sense that

00:47.960 --> 00:53.320
you go and translate your data and the table structure into another language.

00:53.320 --> 01:00.000
So for example, instead of giving access to the table orders, we can create another view called Stellung.

01:00.040 --> 01:01.400
That's the order in German.

01:01.400 --> 01:07.610
But not only you are giving a new name for the object, you could go as well and rename all the columns

01:07.610 --> 01:09.010
inside the view.

01:09.090 --> 01:14.450
Then the German users can access the German view and it's going to be for them, easier to understand

01:14.450 --> 01:16.130
the content of your database.

01:16.170 --> 01:19.210
The same thing for the Indian team and for the Indian users.

01:19.210 --> 01:22.370
You can go and provide a view in Hindi.

01:22.410 --> 01:27.890
I'm not sure whether I'm pronouncing that word correctly, but this is the first word that I said in

01:27.890 --> 01:28.250
Hindi.

01:28.290 --> 01:33.250
I don't promise that I'm going to learn the Hindi language because it's enough to learn Germany.

01:33.250 --> 01:36.370
So I'm trying as well to write this word adesh.

01:36.890 --> 01:38.050
I hope it is correct.

01:38.050 --> 01:42.290
And to be honest, it is really interesting how you write this word in Hindi.

01:42.290 --> 01:43.730
So now back to the topic.

01:43.890 --> 01:50.450
As you can see now we are using like the views in order to provide a translation for our database by

01:50.450 --> 01:54.090
just giving a new name for the views and as well for the columns.

01:54.090 --> 01:59.250
So this is another nice use case that I usually use as well in my projects, in order to provide multi

01:59.250 --> 02:04.050
languages for the data model that I have, and I can do that with the power of views.
